{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/515988-civil-wars","id":515988,"title":"Civil Wars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-16T02:54:48-07:00","id":515988,"title":"Civil Wars","content":"So, I am re-reading Compacts &amp; Conspiracies, and I've noticed that there are many potential group breakdowns and Civil Wars. The Secret Keepers from Network-0, the Rationalist vs the Open Minded in Null Mysteriis, the Sword vs the Scroll in the AKD, the Ascending Ones as whole, the Lucfuge (who may have broken once from the L'Enfant Diabolique) with the Truth vs and the Denial (who may reveal that not of them share the same bloodline), Task Force VALKYRIE who may turn upon itself and of course- the MM, whose Civil War may effect the other orgs more then they expect.<br /> <br /> So- how would you deal with those Civil Wars? Which would come true? Who will survive? Are the groups going to turn into a number of smaller ones, one would devour the other or that the organization itself would fall apart as monsters would use the opportunity to get rid of their old enemies? And most important then all- how would does Civil Wars may effect the other members of the Vigil- for as older groups may fall, new ones can take their place.<br /> <br /> your thoughts on the matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 05-16-2015, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T06:38:28-07:00","id":516130,"title":"","content":"The Rationalist vs Open Minds was a bit silly IMO. It would probably end up with them splitting into two groups with a lot of hurt tempers and no violence. It's not like they actually have much money or resources to fight for.<br /> <br /> My AKD drops the fanaticism angle in favour of an Da Vinci Code like focus on the long game, secrets behind historical events, and a proactive mission to find and reclaim the Relics that will let them reclaim their lost magic. So no civil war there.<br /> <br /> The MM on the other hand I have a personal future cannon for.<br /> <br /> Gallaher is the Irish Archbishop Emeritus of New York City; so I'd say his powerbase is strongest in the USA, Canada and Ireland. When the civil war strikes the Brotherhood of St. Athanasius scores major victories in those areas. The Order of St. Longinus is crushed, it's members either killed or driven from the region. The Order of St. Ambrose is also destroyed, but with far less zeal, most of it's members survive with some being conscripted into the Brotherhood of St. Athanasius but most of them successfuly flee the country while the Athanasians are occupied with the Order of St. Longinus. However without the backing of the church or a restraining hand on the fanacticism the Brotherhood draws unwanted attention from VALKARIE and monsters. It is destroyed within a decade.<br /> <br /> However there is a Dark Horse victory. A lot of Ambrosians don't want to flee their country or join the Brotherhood of St. Athanasius. Which means a sizeable amount of Irish Ambrosians end up in the Sons of CuChulainn. Since these are Athanasiusans they naturally join the Song of Erin. Still stinging from the Athanasius betrayal of the church, and of Catholic values, the ex-Ambrosians fall in love with the idea of using oaths to keep a conspiracy true to it's purpose and develop a hybrid Endowment (think oaths as a conduit for divine power). As the Brotherhood of St. Athanasius looses ground they're poised to fill much of the void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-16-2015, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T11:03:04-07:00","id":516328,"title":"","content":"So it seems that your AKD has already went through its Civil War, and that the scroll won! :P<br /> <br /> Also, I really dig your idea from the MM's Civil War consequences. What would happen in places the Order of Longinus is stronger, like Latin Europe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T11:45:33-07:00","id":516367,"title":"","content":"They'd have some dark days, but they'd recover and end up business as usual. The relatively stronger Ambrosians might take the edge of their fanaticism, it's not like that immortal ghoul is particularly fanatical about witches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T14:16:30-07:00","id":516451,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure. Personally, I'd lean towards having civil wars be the end for C&amp;Cs generally. However, a lot of them have reallly really long histories which makes their breakups kinda implausible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Rationalist vs Open Minds was a bit silly IMO. It would probably end up with them splitting into two groups with a lot of hurt tempers and no violence. It's not like they actually have much money or resources to fight for. </div> </div> </div>I think that's right.<br /> <br /> The MM I'd see just breaking up. The Catholic church doesn't have the reach to actually do much if one secret group wanders off. Lots of secret sects all claiming legitimacy from a Pope who doesn't publicly announce that legitimacy... It's just a mess without an immortal guiding it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T16:21:53-07:00","id":516531,"title":"","content":"Nah. Gallaher is specifically out to get their leader for being a ghoul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T16:30:56-07:00","id":516537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/515988-civil-wars?p=516130#post516130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rationalist vs Open Minds was a bit silly IMO. It would probably end up with them splitting into two groups with a lot of hurt tempers and no violence. It's not like they actually have much money or resources to fight for.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://www.sfjohnson.com/acad/quotescartoons/eraserfightfarsided.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Seeing how some professors treat grad students...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T00:55:44-07:00","id":516852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nah. Gallaher is specifically out to get their leader for being a ghoul. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it would last forever. My point is that Baudolino being immortal provides a stability of leadership over the centuries that keeps the group together (or at least, I think it's a plausible reason for that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T10:04:18-07:00","id":517109,"title":"","content":"As much as I like the organization, I feel like the Union has some of the greatest potential for small-scale civil war between various cells due to how they decide to pursue the Vigil. The Political faction alone can probably cause a lot of tension in an area that doesn't exactly share that worldview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T18:17:01-07:00","id":518627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/515988-civil-wars?p=516130#post516130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rationalist vs Open Minds was a bit silly IMO. It would probably end up with them splitting into two groups with a lot of hurt tempers and no violence. It's not like they actually have much money or resources to fight for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and the entire MO of Null Mysteriis is really quite silly. I keep reading the entries for it over and over and screaming in my head &quot;that's not how science works, that's now how any science works!&quot; There's a section in the Rationalists discussion where the writers use &quot;blah blah blah&quot; and it did pretty much the same thing that finding out supernaturals secretly run all Hunter orgs did - completely disregard the text and utilize theme alone. Would be super nice if the people writing it knew how science worked, but hey, it's hard enough to get that in TV, despite how mind-boggingly simple it all really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T03:16:44-07:00","id":519227,"title":"","content":"They seemed pretty plausible to me for what they are. The NM are dealing with phenomena that are way outside their initial frame of reference. They're pretty up front that a lot of their ideas are wild speculation.<br /> <br /> I really don't get the problem with the blahblahblah comment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T13:09:52-07:00","id":519943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/515988-civil-wars?p=519227#post519227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They seemed pretty plausible to me for what they are. The NM are dealing with phenomena that are way outside their initial frame of reference. They're pretty up front that a lot of their ideas are wild speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Scientific investigation <i>only </i>utilizes a frame of reference if the phenomena is well-documented. Otherwise, you're always treading new ground. The entries for Null Mysteriis keep telling us that &quot;you can't SCIENCE the SUPERNATURAL lol scientists are all pants-on head idiots who think they describe the SUPERNATURAL lolololol&quot; when, you know, any beginning student understands that science is a process, and if you can't apply the scientific method to the supernatural YOU CAN'T MAKE ENDOWMENTS. PERIOD. And definitely not Advanced Armory.<br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis is a perfectly plausible idea, but the implementation isn't plausible at all because whoever is writing it has no idea how the scientific process works. Either that, or they don't care. Full stop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don't get the problem with the blahblahblah comment. </div> </div> </div>See above. It shows flippant disregard for people who are literally paid to use their imagination and the kind of hate I expect from an oWoD supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T17:03:47-07:00","id":520209,"title":"","content":"Basically, if it exists and it is repeatable in some fashion then you can apply the scientific method to it, full stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T19:30:55-07:00","id":520359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/515988-civil-wars?p=520209#post520209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, if it exists and it is repeatable in some fashion then you can apply the scientific method to it, full stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't even have to be repeatable! It just has to affect something we can observe. See: the Big Bang, imaginary time, and prediction of the Higgs effect.<br /> <br /> Heck, imaginary time is a great example - we used it because it makes singularity math work, and now it's looking like it's actually how singularities <i>really </i>work. If scientists have to add superfluous dimensions and universes to make their math work, <i>they will</i>, and when it turns out those superfluous dimensions and universes exist, they will be right there, shining a light down at the monsters and explaining to them exactly how they work, because they predicted it all.<br /> <br /> In fact, that's a great angle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">The Eye (\u25cf to \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">The true benefit of science is its ability to make predictions based upon what has come before. As you've hunter, you've gathered a wide body of knowledge. There are stories you don't believe, but you know enough about strange things not to laugh at them. Those in many practical science fields such as biology, geology, and paleontology have a tendency to refer to this as \u201cthe eye,\u201d which emerges very quickly over the course of a student's career. To the untrained, the ability to pick out a pterosaur bone fragment out of a pile of postage-stamp sized stones or the ability to find a particular type of quartz in a pile of dirty rocks is outright mystical, and the ability to spot something odd and make extremely focused educated guesses is a particularly potent tool in a hunter's arsenal. At the beginning of a scene, you may roll Wits + Science + The Eye to quickly process and collate information you've pieced together from fragmentary reports and precious research. Successes on this roll grants you a pool of dice you can use in Tactics or Perception rolls to notice supernatural details as your ability to predict changes in the behavior of elements in that scene. The hunter can use these dice herself or gift them to nearby hunters, and may either only spend a single die on any given roll, or empty the entire pool.<br /> <br /> Science isn't a cudgel or a wrench that stops working the instant you find a flathead screw - it's that little shapeshifting critter from Treasure Planet that literally turns into whatever tool you can <i>imagine</i>.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","user":"raygungoth","date":". 05-19-2015, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T20:56:22-07:00","id":520390,"title":"","content":"So is there still the chance to have this split in methodology though? Not that the Rationalists are full-on blinders wearing, &quot;LALALA THE ONLY WAY IS MY WAY LALALA&quot;, but more along the lines of, &quot;We need to be more rigorous in our testing and data gathering&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T21:39:08-07:00","id":520423,"title":"","content":"Oh, definitely - you would have a lot of people within the movement itself quibbling hardcore over methods. I've seen two guys get into a fistfight over whether some postage-stamp sized fragments of a jawbone were from mammal-like reptiles or reptile-like mammals. There was blood. At least two broken fingers. It was horrible.<br /> <br /> My guess is that you'd have two orgs, you'd have Null Mysteriis, which is full of scientists who all have different ideas (that work) about how to solve mass conversion problems or do expeditions into shadow and regularly get into bloody, physical fights - there's no academia or journal oversight to reign these bastards in - over whether to label spirits using extant terminology or creating a new vocabulary.<br /> <br /> Then you'd have the &quot;presuppositionalists.&quot; Really once a scientist starts with a random conclusion and then starts looking for just that conclusion they're not a scientist anymore. You'd get people in this camp saying they're members, but they wouldn't be members - they'd be a whole other compact, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}